		(property "Note" "EXTERNAL I2C BUFFER - TCA9517A REPLACED BY THE TCA4307 AT FBV2-S1-009 (O-4 APPROVED). TI TCA4307DGKR, LCSC C880333, VSSOP DGK-8; verified live 2026-08-23 per D-096: 3248 in stock, $2.51 @1 / $1.71 @1k. WHY THE CHANGE: the community port is inherently HOT-PLUG and the external segment is 3.3 V ONLY, so the TCA9517A's level translation was never used while its hot-insertion and stuck-bus weaknesses were. WHAT THE TCA4307 ADDS, from SCPS270B: (1) the IN side is not connected to the OUT side until a STOP or bus-idle condition, so live insertion cannot corrupt a transfer; (2) 1 V PRECHARGE on all four SDA/SCL pins, VPRE 0.8/1/1.2 V; (3) STUCK BUS RECOVERY - SDAOUT or SCLOUT held low for tSTUCKBUS = 25 ms MIN / 40 ms typ / 65 ms MAX disconnects the bus and then issues UP TO 16 PULSES on SCLOUT at 5.5/8.5/14 kHz; (4) POWERED-OFF HIGH-IMPEDANCE I2C pins. VCC = ACC_3V3_SW, so with the accessory rail off the part is unpowered and INVISIBLE TO THE INTERNAL BUS on both sides - that is the isolation guarantee, not a firmware promise. EN = ACC_PWR_EN, active HIGH, VIH 0.7 x VCC, held LOW by `R17` 100 k on sheet 08 so the buffer is ISOLATED until firmware explicitly enables it - the safe state does not depend on the PCAL9535A reset state alone. Supports clock stretching, arbitration and synchronisation. fSCL MAX 400 kHz: THIS IS A FAST-MODE PART, NOT 1 MHz. ICC 2.5 mA typ / 4.5 mA max active, ISD 10 uA typ / 30 uA max in shutdown, UVLO 2.1 V rising. THE CIRCULAR DEPENDENCY IS BROKEN: a wedged accessory used to require the MCU to command the PCAL over the very bus that was wedged; the TCA4307 now disconnects and clocks the bus free autonomously, and ACC_PWR_EN is a second, manual lever rather than the only one. ACCESSORY COMPATIBILITY RULE: an accessory must NEVER hold SDA or SCL low for longer than 25 ms - the tSTUCKBUS MINIMUM - or the buffer will disconnect it. That forbids clock stretching beyond 25 ms and forbids slow bit-banged accessory firmware."
			(at 0 0 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
