			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
		(property "Note" "EXTERNAL I2C SDA pull-up, RE-DERIVED FBV2-S1-009. THE INHERITED 4.7 kOhm IS REJECTED. Rise time is tr = 0.8473 x R x C. At the design-point external capacitance of 200 pF - roughly 20 pF of board trace, 5 pF of connector, about 100 pF for 300 mm of accessory cable and 50 pF of accessory module - 4.7 k gives 796 ns against the 300 ns FAST-MODE limit, i.e. it FAILS 400 kHz by 2.7x and only ever worked at 100 kHz. 1.5 kOhm gives 254 ns and PASSES FAST MODE ON THE STATIC PULL-UP ALONE, with the TCA4307's 2-5 mA rise-time accelerator as margin rather than as the mechanism. Static sink to 0.4 V is 1.93 mA, comfortably inside the 3 mA an I2C device must sink and inside the buffer's 4 mA VOL condition. PUBLISHED ACCESSORY RULE: keep the total external bus capacitance at or below 200 pF for 400 kHz operation and at or below 400 pF for the 100 kHz bring-up mode, where 1.5 k gives 508 ns against a 1000 ns budget. IT IS PULLED TO ACC_3V3_SW, so it disappears with the accessory rail. THE INTERNAL BUS KEEPS ITS OWN AND ONLY PAIR, `R19`/`R20` 2.2 k (D-139) - no second internal pull-up pair is added."
			(at 0 0 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
