	(text "COMMUNITY EXPANSION PORT - AQROOT DEMO SCHEMATIC ECO\n\nJ5 = 24-CONTACT ORDER-B PHYSICAL INTERFACE\n\n 1 5V    2 GND   3 3V3   4 SDA   5 SCL   6 GND   7 NATIVE_A   8 NATIVE_B\n 9 NC   10 NC   11 NC   12 NC   13 XGPIO4 14 XGPIO5 15 NC       16 NC\n17 NC   18 NC   19 GND  20 WAKE 21 DET   22 3V3   23 GND      24 5V\n\nAQROOT DEMO EXPOSES ONLY XGPIO4 AND XGPIO5. CONTACTS 9-12 AND 15-18\nARE EXPLICITLY NC. BOTH SWITCHED-RAIL CONTACT PAIRS SHARE THEIR EXISTING\nTOTAL CURRENT LIMIT. COMMUNITY LOGIC IS 3.3 V; 5 V CONTACTS ARE POWER ONLY."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 76.2 200.66 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "fb090108-0901-4908-9908-00000000017b")
	)
	(text "ACCESSORY DETECT - D-085\n\nTHE ACCESSORY SHORTS PIN 23 TO THE ADJACENT GND AT PIN 21\nWITH ONE 0 OHM LINK. AQROOT PROVIDES THE 100 k PULL-UP,\nWHICH LIVES AT THE EXPANDER AS R129 ON SHEET 08 - THERE IS\nDELIBERATELY NO SECOND PULL-UP HERE.\n\nDETECTION WORKS WITH BOTH ACCESSORY RAILS OFF, BECAUSE THE\nPULL-UP AND THE PCAL BOTH RUN FROM +3V3. THAT IS WHAT MAKES\nMX-3 IMPLEMENTABLE - NEITHER RAIL MAY BE ENABLED UNLESS\nACC_DETECT_N IS ASSERTED - AND IT IS WHAT MAKES A FLIPPED\nACCESSORY PASSIVELY SAFE: IT CANNOT GROUND PIN 23, SO IT\nNEVER RECEIVES POWER.\n\nHOT-PLUG BOUNCE: A MECHANICAL CONTACT WIPING INTO A 100 k\nPULL-UP WILL CHATTER FOR A FEW MILLISECONDS. IT IS DEBOUNCED\nIN FIRMWARE - 20 ms TO ASSERT, 20 ms TO DE-ASSERT - AND NOT\nWITH AN RC. AN RC IS ACTIVELY HARMFUL HERE: THE SAME TIME\nCONSTANT THAT SUPPRESSES INSERTION CHATTER ALSO DELAYS\n*REMOVAL* DETECTION, AND REMOVAL IS THE SAFETY-CRITICAL EDGE\nBECAUSE MX-6 REQUIRES BOTH RAILS DOWN WITHIN 100 ms OF\nDETECT LOSS. 100 k x ANY USEFUL C IS THE WRONG TRADE.\nFIRMWARE DEBOUNCE IS ASYMMETRIC AND FREE."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 220.98 200.66 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "fb090108-0901-4908-9908-00000000017c")
	)
	(text "ACCESSORY POWER SEQUENCING - CTO RULING, FBV2-S1-009\n\nTHE SINGLE ACC_5V_EN IS SPLIT INTO TWO INDEPENDENT ENABLES:\n  U3  P13  ACC_5V_BOOST_EN  -> TPS61023 EN   (U21, SHEET 01)\n  U3  P03  ACC_5V_SW_EN     -> TPS22950C ON  (U22, SHEET 01)\nBOTH CARRY THEIR OWN 100 k EXTERNAL PULL-DOWN, SO BOTH ARE\nOFF BEFORE FIRMWARE RUNS. THE TWO 5 V CONTROLS REMAIN INDEPENDENT.\n\nPOWER-UP:\n  1  VERIFY ACC_DETECT_N ASSERTED\n  2  ACC_3V3_EN  = 1\n  3  WAIT >= 5 ms                       (MX-4)\n  4  ACC_5V_BOOST_EN = 1\n  5  WAIT >= 5 ms FOR THE CONVERTER      (SEE BELOW)\n  6  ACC_5V_SW_EN = 1\n\nPOWER-DOWN, EXACTLY REVERSED:\n  1  ACC_5V_SW_EN = 0\n  2  ACC_5V_BOOST_EN = 0\n  3  ACC_3V3_EN = 0\n\nSTEP 5 IS DERIVED, NOT GUESSED. SLVSDK9: THE TPS61023 SOFT\nSTART IS 700 us TYPICAL FROM EN HIGH TO THE OUTPUT REACHING\nTARGET. THE DATASHEET GIVES NO MAXIMUM, SO THE FIRST BUILD\nUSES 5 ms - SEVEN TIMES TYPICAL - AND IT IS MEASURED ON THE\nFIRST BOARDS. THE SPLIT MAKES THAT NUMBER TRUSTWORTHY: WITH\nU22 STILL OFF THE BOOST STARTS INTO A KNOWN 44 uF OF C65/C66\nAND NOT INTO AN UNKNOWN ACCESSORY, SO THE START-UP TIME IS A\nBOARD CONSTANT INSTEAD OF AN ACCESSORY VARIABLE.\n\nWHAT THE SPLIT BUYS: TWO INDEPENDENT SERIES DISCONNECTS IN\nTHE 5 V PATH. THE TPS61023 HAS TRUE INPUT-TO-OUTPUT\nDISCONNECTION IN SHUTDOWN, SO ACC_5V_RAW REALLY GOES TO ZERO,\nAND THE TPS22950C ADDS REVERSE-CURRENT BLOCKING ON TOP. A\nSINGLE STUCK ENABLE CAN NO LONGER ENERGISE THE CONTACT, AND\nTHE BOOST NO LONGER HAS TO START INTO A HOT-PLUGGED LOAD.\n\nDETECT LOSS OR FLT STILL FORCES A PROMPT SHUTDOWN (MX-5,\nMX-6). NO PGOOD IC IS ADDED FOR THIS."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 76.2 262.89 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "fb090108-0901-4908-9908-00000000017d")
	)
	(text "EXTERNAL I2C - TCA4307, O-4 APPROVED\n\nU16 TCA9517ADGK -> TI TCA4307DGKR (LCSC C880333).\nIN SIDE  = I2C_SDA_INT / I2C_SCL_INT  (INTERNAL BUS)\nOUT SIDE = EXT_SDA / EXT_SCL          (ACCESSORY SEGMENT)\nVCC = ACC_3V3_SW, SO THE PART IS UNPOWERED AND HIGH-Z ON\nBOTH SIDES WHENEVER THE ACCESSORY RAIL IS OFF.\nEN = ACC_PWR_EN, HELD LOW BY R17 100 k ON SHEET 08.\n\nTIMING THAT AN ACCESSORY MUST RESPECT:\n  tSTUCKBUS  25 ms MIN / 40 ms TYP / 65 ms MAX\n  RECOVERY   UP TO 16 SCL PULSES AT 5.5 / 8.5 / 14 kHz\n  PRECHARGE  0.8 / 1.0 / 1.2 V\n  fSCL       400 kHz MAX - FAST MODE, **NOT** 1 MHz\n\nACCESSORY RULE: NEVER HOLD SDA OR SCL LOW LONGER THAN 25 ms.\nTHAT IS THE STUCK-BUS MINIMUM, AND IT FORBIDS CLOCK\nSTRETCHING OR BIT-BANGING BEYOND IT.\n\nPULL-UPS: R49/R50 1.5 k TO ACC_3V3_SW. THE INHERITED 4.7 k\nWAS WRONG - 796 ns AT THE 200 pF DESIGN POINT AGAINST A\n300 ns FAST-MODE BUDGET. 1.5 k GIVES 254 ns ON THE STATIC\nPULL-UP ALONE. THE INTERNAL BUS KEEPS R19/R20 2.2 k AS ITS\nONLY PAIR (D-139); NOTHING IS ADDED THERE.\n\nADDRESSING IS NOT ISOLATED - THE TWO SEGMENTS ARE ONE\nADDRESS SPACE WHENEVER THE RAIL IS ON. THAT IS DELIBERATE:\nP-18 IS CLOSED WITH NO MUX. THE BUFFER SOLVES *ELECTRICAL*\nFAULT ISOLATION; I2C_ADDRESS_REGISTRY.md SOLVES ADDRESSES."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 220.98 262.89 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "fb090108-0901-4908-9908-00000000017e")
	)
