		(property "Note_Sourcing" "SOURCING D-614. REFERENCE_RULING from the beta-dm audit line 'J8' (SOURCING-LEDGER); manufacturer named with the part in SOURCING_LEDGER; D-238, recorded in docs/full-beta-v2/assembly/SOURCING_LEDGER.md s.2 (JST SH, 1.0 mm, 4 circuit, side entry, SMT, 1.0 A, 50 V) and in DEVICE_SPEC s.10.2, which also lists the absent schematic property as an open item.  The plating-suffixed string is the one D-096 requires: the bare order code resolves to a zero-stock listing."
			(at 176.53 133.35 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
		(property "Description" "Qwiic / STEMMA QT I2C connector, JST SM04B-SRSS-TB(LF)(SN), SH series 1.0 mm pitch, 4 circuit, SIDE ENTRY, surface mount, body 6.0 x 4.25 mm, 1.0 A, 50 V AC/DC, -25 to +85 C, contact resistance 20 mOhm initial. ADDED AT FBV2-EXP-002 (D-238). PIN ORDER IS THE ECOSYSTEM STANDARD, NOT A CHOICE: 1 GND (black), 2 3.3 V (red), 3 SDA (blue), 4 SCL (yellow) - identical for SparkFun Qwiic and Adafruit STEMMA QT, so every cable in either ecosystem mates it. IT ADDS NO COMPONENT: it lands on the PROTECTED EXTERNAL segment at EXT_SDA / EXT_SCL, downstream of U16 TCA4307 and of the R47/R48 22 ohm series pair and at D2's TPD4E1B06 clamp, so it inherits the hot-swap buffer, the R49/R50 1.5 k pull-ups, the series resistance and the ESD array. POWER IS ACC_3V3_SW AND THAT IS ARCHITECTURAL, NOT A PREFERENCE: U16's own VCC is already ACC_3V3_SW and the pull-ups pull to it, so feeding the port from unswitched +3V3 would create a powered-device / unpowered-bus state and invite back-feeding through the accessory's ESD diodes. ACC_5V_SW IS NEVER EXPOSED HERE."
			(at 176.53 133.35 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
