	(text "QWIIC / STEMMA QT - FBV2-EXP-002 (D-238)\n\nJ8 = JST SM04B-SRSS-TB(LF)(SN), SH 1.0 mm, 4 circuit,\nSIDE ENTRY SMT. 1 GND / 2 3V3 / 3 SDA / 4 SCL is the\nECOSYSTEM STANDARD ORDER - Qwiic and STEMMA QT are\nidentical here, so every cable in either ecosystem mates.\n\nIT ADDS NO COMPONENT. It taps the PROTECTED EXTERNAL\nsegment at EXT_SDA / EXT_SCL - downstream of U16 and of\nthe R47/R48 22 R pair, at D2's clamp - so it inherits the\nhot-swap buffer, the R49/R50 1.5 k pull-ups, the series\nresistance and the ESD array. NO second buffer, NO mux,\nNO repeater, NO extra pull-ups, NO second TVS.\n\nPOWER = ACC_3V3_SW, ARCHITECTURAL NOT PREFERENTIAL:\nU16's own VCC is already ACC_3V3_SW and the pull-ups pull\nto it, so an unswitched +3V3 feed would create a\npowered-device / unpowered-bus state.\n\nACC_5V_SW IS NEVER EXPOSED ON QWIIC.\n\nBUS BUDGET: <= 200 pF at 400 kHz on the 1.5 k pull-ups.\nOn-board copper ~20 pF + connector ~1 pF + a 100 mm cable\n~5-10 pF + a typical breakout ~10 pF; three daisy-chained\nboards ~55-75 pF. 100 kHz remains the fallback."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 163.0 108.0 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fb090108-0901-4908-9908-000000000940")
	)
